#: ../../getting_started/installation/singleNode/redhat.rst:2
msgid "Single Node Install on RHEL"
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/installation/singleNode/redhat.rst:4
msgid ""
"To get started installing |morpheus| on RHEL/RedHat a few prerequisite "
"items are required."
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/installation/singleNode/redhat.rst:6
msgid ""
"Choose whether the appliance or your organization will manage the host "
"firewall. See `RHEL firewall behavior`_ before the first reconfigure."
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/installation/singleNode/redhat.rst:7
msgid "Make sure the machine is self resolvable to its own hostname."
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/installation/singleNode/redhat.rst:8
msgid ""
"For RHEL 7.x, the Optional RPMs repo needs to be added for Reconfigure to"
" succeed. It does not need to be added For RHEL 8.x, as the Optional RPMs"
" repo is now part of the appstream repo that is enabled by default in "
"RHEL 8.x."
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/installation/singleNode/redhat.rst:10
msgid ""
"**RHEL 7.x Amazon:** ``yum-config-manager --enable rhel-7-server-rhui-"
"optional-rpms``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/installation/singleNode/redhat.rst:11
msgid "**RHEL 7.x:** ``yum-config-manager --enable rhel-7-server-optional-rpms``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/installation/singleNode/redhat.rst:13
#: ../../getting_started/installation/singleNode/redhat.rst:67
#: ../../getting_started/installation/singleNode/redhat.rst:112
msgid "Note"
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/installation/singleNode/redhat.rst:13
msgid ""
"For Amazon users a Redhat subscription is not required if the appropriate"
" yum REGION repository is added instead as demonstrated above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/installation/singleNode/redhat.rst:15
msgid ""
"The RedHat Enterprise Linux server needs to be registered and activated "
"with Redhat subscription. The server optional rpms repo needs to be "
"enabled as well."
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/installation/singleNode/redhat.rst:18
msgid "RHEL firewall behavior"
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/installation/singleNode/redhat.rst:20
msgid ""
"By default, ``morpheus-ctl reconfigure`` runs the appliance firewall "
"recipe. On RHEL 7 and later, the recipe stops and disables ``firewalld``,"
" installs the appropriate ``iptables`` services package, enables "
"``iptables``, writes the appliance IPv4 rules, and links them at "
"``/etc/sysconfig/iptables``. The default input policy generated by the "
"appliance is ``ACCEPT``. Review the resulting policy before exposing the "
"host to an untrusted network."
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/installation/singleNode/redhat.rst:22
msgid ""
"To retain a customer-managed firewall such as ``firewalld``, add the "
"following to ``/etc/morpheus/morpheus.rb`` **before the first "
"reconfigure**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/installation/singleNode/redhat.rst:24
msgid ""
"firewall['enabled'] = false\n"
"firewall['ipv4'] = false"
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/installation/singleNode/redhat.rst:29
msgid ""
"``firewall['enabled'] = false`` prevents the firewall recipe from "
"running. Setting only ``firewall['ipv4'] = false`` is not sufficient to "
"retain ``firewalld`` because the RHEL portion of the enabled recipe still"
" manages the firewall services. After disabling appliance firewall "
"management, configure the required rules with your organization's "
"firewall tooling. Use the canonical :ref:`Ports and Protocols <ports-and-"
"protocols>` table to determine which ports apply to the deployment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/installation/singleNode/redhat.rst:31
msgid "Warning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/installation/singleNode/redhat.rst:33
msgid ""
"Disabling appliance firewall management does not create, validate, or "
"preserve a customer firewall policy. Validate access from an "
"administrative session before disconnecting, and maintain the policy "
"through your normal operating-system configuration process. Do not rely "
"on custom ``iptables`` changes surviving a later reconfigure or upgrade."
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/installation/singleNode/redhat.rst:35
msgid ""
"To check if the server has been activated please run the subscription-"
"manager version. Subscription manager will return the version plus the "
"python dependency version."
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/installation/singleNode/redhat.rst:37
msgid ""
"If the server has not been registered and activated then the subscription"
" manager version will return the below message."
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/installation/singleNode/redhat.rst:39
msgid ""
"sudo subscription-manager version\n"
"server type: This system is currently not registered\n"
"subscription management server: 0.9.51.24.-1\n"
"subscription-manager: 1.10.14-7.el7 python-rhsm: 1.10.12-2.el7"
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/installation/singleNode/redhat.rst:46
msgid ""
"When a server has been registered and activated with Redhat the "
"subscription manager will return the below message."
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/installation/singleNode/redhat.rst:48
msgid ""
"sudo subscription-manager version\n"
"server type: Red Hat Subscription Management\n"
"subscription management server: 0.9.51.24-1\n"
"subscription-manager: 1.10.14-7.el7 python-rhsm: 1.10.12-2.el7"
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/installation/singleNode/redhat.rst:55
msgid ""
"If the subscription manager re-turns the message ``This system is "
"currently not registered`` please follow the below steps to register the "
"server."
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/installation/singleNode/redhat.rst:57
#: ../../getting_started/installation/singleNode/redhat.rst:78
#: ../../getting_started/installation/singleNode/redhat.rst:95
#: ../../getting_started/installation/singleNode/redhat.rst:120
msgid "Tip"
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/installation/singleNode/redhat.rst:57
msgid ""
"To register the server you will need to have sudo permissions [Member of "
"the Wheel group] or root access to the server. You will also need your "
"Redhat registered email address and password."
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/installation/singleNode/redhat.rst:59
msgid "subscription-manager register"
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/installation/singleNode/redhat.rst:61
msgid ""
"sudo subscription-manager register\n"
"Username: redhat@example.com\n"
"Password: . subscription-manager auto --attach"
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/installation/singleNode/redhat.rst:67
msgid "This can take a minute to complete"
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/installation/singleNode/redhat.rst:69
msgid ""
"sudo subscription-manager attach --auto\n"
"\n"
"Installed Product Current Status: Product Name: Red Hat Enterprise Linux\n"
"Server Status: Subscribed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/installation/singleNode/redhat.rst:76
msgid ""
"To check to see if the RHEL server has the Red Hat Enterprise Linux 7 "
"Server - Optional (RPMs) repo enabled please run the following command to"
" return the repo status."
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/installation/singleNode/redhat.rst:78
msgid ""
"To check the server repos you will need to have sudo permissions [Member "
"of the Wheel group] or root access to the server."
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/installation/singleNode/redhat.rst:80
msgid ""
"sudo yum repolist all | grep \"rhel-7-server-optional-rpms\" rhel-7"
"-server-optional-rpms/7Server/x86_64 disabled"
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/installation/singleNode/redhat.rst:84
msgid ""
"If the repo status was returned as disabled then you will need to enable "
"the repo using the subscription manager like below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/installation/singleNode/redhat.rst:86
msgid ""
"sudo subscription-manager repos --enable rhel-7-server-optional-rpms\n"
"Repository 'rhel-7-server-optional-rpms' is enabled for this system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/installation/singleNode/redhat.rst:91
msgid ""
"The message ``Repo 'rhel-7-server-optional-rpms' is enabled for this "
"system.`` will appear after enabling the repo. This will confirm that the"
" repo has been enabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/installation/singleNode/redhat.rst:93
msgid ""
"Next simply download the relevant ``.rpm`` package for installation. This"
" package can be acquired from morpheushub.com."
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/installation/singleNode/redhat.rst:95
msgid ""
"Use the ``wget`` command to directly download the package to your "
"appliance server. i.e. ``wget "
"https://downloads.morpheusdata.com/path/to/package.rpm``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/installation/singleNode/redhat.rst:97
msgid ""
"Next we must install the package onto the machine and configure the "
"morpheus services:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/installation/singleNode/redhat.rst:99
msgid ""
"sudo rpm -i morpheus-appliance_x.x.x-1_amd64.rpm\n"
"sudo morpheus-ctl reconfigure"
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/installation/singleNode/redhat.rst:104
msgid ""
"Once the installation is complete the web interface will automatically "
"start up. By default it will be resolvable at "
"``https://your_machine_name`` and in many cases this may not be "
"resolvable from your browser. The url can be changed by editing "
"``/etc/morpheus/morpheus.rb`` and changing the value of "
"``appliance_url``. After this has been changed simply run:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/installation/singleNode/redhat.rst:106
msgid ""
"sudo morpheus-ctl reconfigure\n"
"sudo morpheus-ctl stop morpheus-ui\n"
"sudo morpheus-ctl start morpheus-ui"
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/installation/singleNode/redhat.rst:112
msgid ""
"The ``morpheus-ui`` can take 2-3 minutes to startup before it becomes "
"available."
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/installation/singleNode/redhat.rst:114
msgid ""
"There are additional install settings that can be viewed in the "
":ref:`additional_options` section."
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/installation/singleNode/redhat.rst:116
msgid ""
"Once the browser is pointed to the appliance a first time setup wizard "
"will be presented. Please follow the on screen instructions by creating "
"the master account. From there you will be presented with the license "
"settings page where a license can be applied for use (if a license is "
"required you may request one or purchase one by contacting your sales "
"representative)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/installation/singleNode/redhat.rst:118
msgid ""
"More details on setting up infrastructure can be found throughout this "
"guide."
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/installation/singleNode/redhat.rst:120
msgid ""
"If any issues occur it may be prudent to check the morpheus log for "
"details at ``/var/log/morpheus/morpheus-ui/current``."
msgstr ""

